diff --git a/docs/android-network-audio.md b/docs/android-network-audio.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..03a4f36
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/android-network-audio.md
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+# Android network-audio pilot
+
+An explicitly selected test transport exchanges continuous, unframed,
+little-endian float32 mono PCM at 8000 Hz over one outbound TCP connection.
+The modem's waveform and host protocols are unchanged. This is a no-radio
+pilot, not a replacement for device audio or RF qualification.
+
+In the Android TNC's Settings, enter a callsign, enable **Network audio
+test (no radio)**, and set the peer host and TCP port. Start on the Modem
+tab, then open Ragtime with host 127.0.0.1, KISS 8100 and command 8300
+(session data 8301). The TNC's foreground service and Qt event loop keep
+running behind Ragtime. Back/Home leave the TNC running; swiping its task
+away still shuts it down. Network audio settings are locked while running.
+
+This mode never opens a rig, microphone or speaker. It uses the Android
+special-use foreground-service type from API 34, with its purpose declared
+in the manifest, and does not request microphone permission. Notification
+permission is requested separately. Ordinary device-audio mode keeps its
+existing permission/service behavior. Saved rig/device choices are not
+replaced by the network mode's runtime overrides.
+
+The desktop host also accepts `--audio-io tcp:HOST:PORT --no-rig`. One
+worker Qt thread owns the socket and a 32 ms playback timer. Partial float
+bytes are retained between reads. RX/TX counters are shown on Android.
+The receive and pending transmit buffers are bounded to about one second.
+Invalid samples, capture loss, queue overflow, connect timeout, ten seconds
+without incoming audio, and disconnect fail explicitly. The owner stops
+the station and closes its client ports; restarting is explicit. No jitter
+correction, clock-drift compensation or automatic reconnect is implemented.
+
+Network test recordings are app-private under `files/network-recordings`.
+The Android build uses the existing `tools/build_android.sh` with matching
+Qt host/Android packages. The pilot used Qt 6.11.1, NDK 27.2.12479018,
+JDK 21, target SDK 36 and ARM64, with `DATA2G_ANDROID_RIG=OFF`.
+
+`native/tests/test_tcp_audio.cpp` checks exact float values and outgoing
+bytes across TCP fragments, counters, peer-disconnect wakeup, and prompt,
+idempotent shutdown. It is included in CTest when `data2g_station` is built.
+The shared core and generated tables are unchanged.
